<title>USA: Anchor Financial stock jumps on stock split.</title>
<headline>Anchor Financial stock jumps on stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MYRTLE BEACH, S.C.</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock of Anchor Financial Corp. jumped Tuesday after the bank holding company said its board of directors approved a three-for-two stock split.</p>
<p>Anchor was up $2 at $37.50 on the Nasdaq market.</p>
<p>The Myrtle Beach. S.C.-based company, which has assets of $544.8 million, said the stock split will take the form of a 50 percent common stock dividend, payable on Sept. 26 to shareholders of record on Aug. 29.</p>
</text>
